  "result": "I fixed the order of the names within each option in `--help`. The cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`, which sorted the option names by prefix length in reverse. Because of that, long names came before short ones, so `--name, -n` was printed instead of `-n, --name`. I removed `reverse=True`, so short names now come first.\n\nI checked this with a small command that has `--name/-n` and `--verbose/-v`. It now prints `-n, --name TEXT` and `-v, --verbose`. The test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). It passed before the fix too, so no existing test covers this ordering, and I didn't add one.\n\nIn that check `--help` is listed last, after the options I defined. Click appends it that way, so I left it alone. If you meant a different ordering problem, such as which options appear first, tell me and I'll look again.",
